{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7404dc97a7898d37","name":"card_event_persian_corridor","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Homefront/events/card_event_persian_corridor","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PERSIAN CORRIDOR","text":"Give a friendly British or US unit: \"Destruction: Trigger all Destruction effects of your Soviet units.\"","flavorText":"The Persian Corridor became the Soviet Union’s most reliable supply line after Germany cut off the northern and western routes. Beginning in 1941, British and American forces moved Lend-Lease materiel through the Persian Gulf and across Iran into the Caucasus. This route carried nearly 8 million long tons of cargo, over 40 percent of all US aid sent to the Soviets. Iran’s roads and railways, many in poor condition before the war, were rapidly upgraded by Allied engineers. New ports and depots were built, and thousands of trucks moved daily convoys through rugged terrain. British and Indian troops managed security in the south, while Soviet units operated in the north. Unlike the Arctic convoys, which were often stalled by German attacks or harsh weather, the Persian Corridor stayed open year-round. The supplies it delivered included tanks, aircraft, food and raw materials critical to Soviet operations on the Eastern Front. It also helped the Allies maintain influence in a strategically important region for the rest of the war.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_persian_corridor","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_persian_corridor_title","SourceString":"PERSIAN CORRIDOR","LocalizedString":"PERSIAN CORRIDOR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_persian_corridor_text","SourceString":"Give a friendly British or US unit: \"Destruction: Trigger all Destruction effects of your Soviet units.\"","LocalizedString":"Give a friendly British or US unit: \"Destruction: Trigger all Destruction effects of your Soviet units.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_persian_corridor_history","SourceString":"The Persian Corridor became the Soviet Union’s most reliable supply line after Germany cut off the northern and western routes. Beginning in 1941, British and American forces moved Lend-Lease materiel through the Persian Gulf and across Iran into the Caucasus. This route carried nearly 8 million long tons of cargo, over 40 percent of all US aid sent to the Soviets. Iran’s roads and railways, many in poor condition before the war, were rapidly upgraded by Allied engineers. New ports and depots were built, and thousands of trucks moved daily convoys through rugged terrain. British and Indian troops managed security in the south, while Soviet units operated in the north. Unlike the Arctic convoys, which were often stalled by German attacks or harsh weather, the Persian Corridor stayed open year-round. The supplies it delivered included tanks, aircraft, food and raw materials critical to Soviet operations on the Eastern Front. It also helped the Allies maintain influence in a strategically important region for the rest of the war.","LocalizedString":"The Persian Corridor became the Soviet Union’s most reliable supply line after Germany cut off the northern and western routes. Beginning in 1941, British and American forces moved Lend-Lease materiel through the Persian Gulf and across Iran into the Caucasus. This route carried nearly 8 million long tons of cargo, over 40 percent of all US aid sent to the Soviets. Iran’s roads and railways, many in poor condition before the war, were rapidly upgraded by Allied engineers. New ports and depots were built, and thousands of trucks moved daily convoys through rugged terrain. British and Indian troops managed security in the south, while Soviet units operated in the north. Unlike the Arctic convoys, which were often stalled by German attacks or harsh weather, the Persian Corridor stayed open year-round. The supplies it delivered included tanks, aircraft, food and raw materials critical to Soviet operations on the Eastern Front. It also helped the Allies maintain influence in a strategically important region for the rest of the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Patriotic_Push'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Patriotic_Push.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/10_Homefront/T_persian_corridor.T_persian_corridor","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/PERSIAN_CORRIDOR.PERSIAN_CORRIDOR","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_persian_corridor_photo","SourceString":"Indian Army soldiers standing next to a supply convoy en route to the Soviet Union, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Indian Army soldiers standing next to a supply convoy en route to the Soviet Union, 1944."},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tmpCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_persian_corridor_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*"